      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village grew into a rural agricultural hub serving farms in the fertile Loess Plains, thanks to its water power from Aowa Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/martinsburg_nebraska",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A post office operated from 1880 until 1967, after which mail was routed from Ponca.",
